0..48 Comment "// Higher-order calls preserve recursive stages."
49..51 Comment "//"
52..117 Comment "// `apply` uses one type parameter for its function and argument."
118..180 Comment "// A call instantiates that parameter at its argument\'s stage."
181..260 Comment "// The run of `count` waits until the machine takes a type code as an argument."
261..263 Comment "//"
264..301 Comment "// `applyAt` quantifies over a stage."
302..346 Comment "// `predAt` returns at its argument\'s stage."
347..395 Comment "// `sameAt` accepts both arguments at one stage."
396..443 Comment "// A named stage must agree with the arguments."
444..495 Comment "// A higher-order use preserves its supplied stage."
496..498 Comment "//"
499..513 Comment "// - see: #393"
514..528 Comment "// - see: #452"
529..543 Comment "// - see: #392"
544..585 Comment "// - see: #1227 — `agreed`, `appliedAt`"
586..616 Comment "// - see: #1498 — `passedAt`"
617..658 Comment "// - see: #2373 — `predAt`, `boundedAt`"
659..694 Comment "// - see: #1241 — `boundedHelped`"
695..771 Comment "// - see: `../../pathological/data/sized-higher-order.gandr` — the checker"
772..850 Comment "//   refuses a `k` not below `j`, a call that no stage fits, and a named stage"
851..886 Comment "//   that the arguments do not show"
888..930 Comment "// The naturals the recursion takes apart."
931..937 Keyword "import"
